detector_raw:
{
  "action": "question",
  "question_count": 1,
  "is_atomic": true,
  "atomic_questions": [
    "What is the objective of this packing plan — are we minimizing the number of containers used, maximizing the total weight (or total units) of goods shipped, or something else?"
  ],
  "rationale": "The response asks for a single policy choice regarding the optimization objective, presenting mutually exclusive options for one decision."
}

{
  "action": "question",
  "question_count": 1,
  "is_atomic": true,
  "atomic_questions": [
    "You said the goal is to pack all the goods — does that mean every available unit of every type (all 120 A, 90 B, 300 C, 90 D, 120 E) must be loaded, or is it acceptable to leave some units unshipped as long as the containers that are used satisfy the rules?"
  ],
  "rationale": "The response asks a single clarification question regarding whether all units must be loaded or if some can be left unshipped."
}

{
  "action": "question",
  "question_count": 1,
  "is_atomic": true,
  "atomic_questions": [
    "Since we minimize the number of containers and it's fine to leave goods unshipped, is there any requirement that a certain amount of goods must actually be shipped (e.g., a minimum total weight or a minimum number of units of some type), or is it acceptable in principle to ship nothing at all if that uses fewer containers?"
  ],
  "rationale": "The response asks a single clarification question regarding whether there is a minimum shipment requirement or if shipping nothing is acceptable."
}

{
  "action": "question",
  "question_count": 1,
  "is_atomic": true,
  "atomic_questions": [
    "Is the number of containers a fixed, given value that we must work with, or is it a decision variable we choose (and minimize) as part of the plan?"
  ],
  "rationale": "The response asks a single clarification question regarding the status of the container count (fixed vs. decision variable)."
}

{
  "action": "question",
  "question_count": 1,
  "is_atomic": true,
  "atomic_questions": [
    "The rule says each container must contain at least 12 units of type D — does this apply to every container that is used, including ones that might otherwise be filled with other goods?"
  ],
  "rationale": "The response contains a single clarification question asking for confirmation on the scope of a specific rule."
}

{
  "action": "question",
  "question_count": 1,
  "is_atomic": true,
  "atomic_questions": [
    "does this \"at least one\" mean at least one unit of C, or at least one full container's worth of C?"
  ],
  "rationale": "The response asks for a single clarification regarding the definition of the quantity 'at least one' in the context of the rule."
}

{
  "action": "question",
  "question_count": 1,
  "is_atomic": true,
  "atomic_questions": [
    "Are the goods units indivisible (each unit must be whole, so the number of units of each type in each container must be an integer), or can units be split fractionally?"
  ],
  "rationale": "The response asks a single clarification question regarding the divisibility of goods units."
}

{
  "action": "question",
  "question_count": 1,
  "is_atomic": true,
  "atomic_questions": [
    "The 18-ton minimum and 60-ton maximum per container — are these strict (a container must be strictly above 18 tons and strictly below 60 tons) or inclusive (exactly 18 tons or exactly 60 tons is allowed)?"
  ],
  "rationale": "The response asks a single clarification question regarding whether the weight limits are strict or inclusive."
}

{
  "action": "question",
  "question_count": 1,
  "is_atomic": true,
  "atomic_questions": [
    "Since the number of containers is a decision variable we minimize, is there any upper bound on how many containers we are allowed to use, or can we use as many as needed?"
  ],
  "rationale": "The response asks a single clarification question regarding the upper bound constraint on the number of containers."
}

{
  "action": "question",
  "question_count": 1,
  "is_atomic": true,
  "atomic_questions": [
    "When a container contains type A and therefore must also contain at least one unit of type C, does that required C unit count toward the container's weight (i.e., it's just a normal C unit that also satisfies the A-triggered requirement), or is it a separate, additional C unit on top of any other C loaded?"
  ],
  "rationale": "The response asks a single clarification question regarding whether a required unit is an additional item or satisfies an existing slot, which constitutes one independent policy choice."
}

{
  "action": "question",
  "question_count": 1,
  "is_atomic": true,
  "atomic_questions": [
    "The minimum of 12 units of D per container — is this a hard requirement that must hold for every used container, or is it a soft target that could be relaxed if doing so allows fewer containers overall?"
  ],
  "rationale": "The response asks for a single policy choice regarding the nature of the minimum unit constraint (hard vs. soft), which constitutes one semantically independent question."
}

{
  "action": "question",
  "question_count": 1,
  "is_atomic": true,
  "atomic_questions": [
    "Is it acceptable for the plan to ship only a subset of the goods (i.e., not all available units) in order to minimize the number of containers, or is there an expectation that we should ship as much as possible?"
  ],
  "rationale": "The response contains a single clarification question asking for a policy choice between minimizing containers (allowing partial shipment) and maximizing shipment volume."
}

{
  "action": "question",
